You can flash the C6 firmware by yourself too. The process is the same as the official Espressif ESP32C6 firmware flashing guide.

The ESP32-C6 firmware can be updated using either of the following methods:

- **UART flashing:** 

  1. Prepare a USB-UART (TTL level) cable, to connect the pins and your computer.
  2. Connect GND (Pin 4) to your UART cable's GND, connect GND to C6_IO9 (Pin 6) to let C6 enter flash mode.
  3. Connect C6_U0TXD (Pin 3) to your cable's RX pin.
  4. Connect C6_U0RXD (Pin 5) to your cable's TX pin. 
  5. Reset the product/C6 to enter download mode, you can unplug all power sources first and then connect USB-C to your power adapter as a reset. 
  6. Remove the C6_IO9 (Pin 6) short to leave flash mode in the next reset.
  7. Reset the product/C6 after flashing to boot normally.
- **Updates through the ESP32-P4:** The ESP32-P4 can flash new firmware to the ESP32-C6 through SDIO using a firmware image if C6 already has a firmware (OTA). This is usually done with a MicroSD card.

